    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files, mini.bracketed\n\n### Description\n\nwhen [opening a new file with mini.bracketed](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.bracketed/blob/daf2bff8172bc84bfb934f765275618f5e7844a8/lua/mini/bracketed.lua#L549) or [renaming a buffer with mini.files](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.files/blob/72cc9045c1011f2c158117bd5a0d339792b7f34a/lua/mini/files.lua#L2810)\r\n, `:buffers` shows the full path instead of a relative path, similar to this https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.files/commit/c52180c7c7e4e35a4c925f429316af41cc412d1a\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. MiniBracketed.file()\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\na relative path is expected to show in `:buffers`\n\n### Actual behavior\n\na full path is shown instead",
